From 6d27ebaef63c0ea2cacf13d3ab4901d5e7fe6475 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: overdoingism <overdoingism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:32:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gdn-conv-store: the one-kernel GDN conv step also takes a
 multi-sequence ubatch (two slots verifying in one batch)

With --kv-unified and several slots, a verify ubatch holds S sequences of T tokens: the state [3, C, S], x^T [T, C, S] (a view of
the in-projection's output [C, T*S]), the window view [3, Kw, C, S] and the slots [3, K, C, S] (the sequences' cells, nb[3]
apart).  The store took S = 1 only, so such a step ran the whole chain on every GDN layer -- GET_ROWS, CONCAT, SET_ROWS,
SSM_CONV, SILU, the norm pair -- the limitation r244 records ("a multi-sequence ubatch still declines").

Now 1..8 sequences, one block row a sequence; T, C and S come from the transposed view (its root is 2-D).  With S > 1 the state
stays the GET_ROWS copy: the gather is deferred for one sequence only, since one sequence's cache rows may be another's
source.  GGML_CUDA_CONV_DEBUG=1: the GDN_CONV_STORE line gains S= and is printed once for each S, so a multi-sequence step
shows up next to the single-sequence ones.  Kill switches unchanged: GGML_CUDA_FUSE_GDN_CONV_STORE=0, or
GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_CONV_FUSION=1 for the whole conv family.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
